==Icelandic==
{{Icelandic declension kk sb 01|hest|ur}}
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hestr}}.

===Noun===
'''hestur''' {{m}}

# [[horse]]

====Synonyms====
*[[hross]], [[klár]]

====Usage notes====
* The noun [[hestur]] is often used to determine the inflection of a noun, as every {{singular}} [[indefinite]] form is [[different]]. This is done either by substituting the word (whose form is unknown) with '''hestur''':
*: ''[[ég#Icelandic|ég]] [[borða]] [[brauð]].'' (I [[eat]] [[bread]])
*:Becomes:
*: ''[[ég#Icelandic|ég]] [[borða]] '''hest'''. (I [[eat]] a [[horse]])
*: And because the word '''hest''' is {{accusative}}, the word ''[[brauð]]'' must here also be {{accusative}}.
* Another way of doing this is putting some common and predetermined 'phrases' in front of the word in question, ''e.g.'':
*: [[hér]] [[vera#Icelandic|er]] '''hestur''' ({{nominative}}) = there is a '''horse''' here (lit. here is a horse)
*: [[um]] '''[[hest]]''' ({{accusative}}) = about a '''horse'''
*: [[frá]] '''[[hesti]]''' ({{dat}}) = from a '''horse'''
*: [[til]] '''[[hests]]''' ({{gen}}) = to a '''horse'''

